I-5 admission-reason probe construction hook (SPEC_common_measurement_v0 sec 9,
2026-10-19).  Wired into sync_engine_tree.sh 2026-10-20 (decision 15, grep guard
"maybe_install_admission_probe", after chunk_probe); it changes scheduler.py
bytes (manifest entry 10) and admission_probe.py is entry 28 -> new ENGINE_DIGEST.

ONE hunk, in run_scheduler_process (module level, after the Scheduler class),
between `Scheduler(...)` construction and `pipe_writer.send(...)`.  All logic
lives in sglang/srt/multiplex/admission_probe.py and installs itself by
wrapping, at class level, PrefillAdder.__init__/add_one_req and
Scheduler.get_new_batch_prefill / get_num_allocatable_reqs /
update_running_batch / _add_request_to_queue / update_split_prefill_batch --
only when PDMUX_ADMISSION_PATH is set.  Unset: the factory returns None, no
wrapper is installed, the engine runs the pristine functions.

WHY HERE.  (1) Arm symmetry: run_scheduler_process is the common entry of the
fused loops and event_loop_pdmux, so the probe is not a pdmux-only hook
(Gate-1 defect).  (2) No line of the Scheduler class moves, so the
fingerprinted citations in scripts/discipline/line_citations.json
(scheduler.py:2309-2313, :2382, :2447, ...) stay valid.  (3) The hunk is far
outside the context windows of holb_probe_scheduler_hooks.patch and
chunk_probe_scheduler_hook.patch, so their reverse-application tests are
unaffected.  Must be applied AFTER those two (its offsets are computed on the
tree they produce).

--- a/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
+++ b/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
@@ -3658,6 +3658,18 @@
             dp_rank,
         )
 
+        # I-5 admission-reason probe (arm-agnostic; default OFF).  Returns None
+        # unless PDMUX_ADMISSION_PATH is set; when set it wraps the admission
+        # entry points of Scheduler / PrefillAdder at class level, so the fused
+        # loops and event_loop_pdmux are instrumented by the same code.  Placed
+        # here (after __init__, before the event loop) so that no line of the
+        # Scheduler class moves.  See sglang/srt/multiplex/admission_probe.py.
+        from sglang.srt.multiplex.admission_probe import (
+            maybe_install_admission_probe,
+        )
+
+        scheduler.admission_probe = maybe_install_admission_probe(scheduler)
+
         # Send initialization info back to the parent process
         pipe_writer.send(scheduler.get_init_info())
 
